mode: "100644"
text: "# Examples — content calendars\n\nTwo worked calendars showing cadence, the recurring skeleton, series, and a sample week — plus an\nover-ambitious version for contrast. Voice in the sample posts is the blunt indie-founder voice from\nearlier skills. Your output uses the loaded `voice.md`, `content-pillars.md`, and `social-strategy.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Example 1 — Solo SaaS founder · 1 primary + 1 secondary platform\n\n**Capacity:** solo, ~4 hrs/week. **Pillars:** A = building in public, B = SaaS lessons, C = the\ncategory POV. **Platforms:** LinkedIn (primary), TikTok (secondary).\n\n**Cadence (sustainable floor):** LinkedIn 3×/week, TikTok 2×/week. (Not daily — held for the long\nrun beats heroic-then-quit.)\n\n**Recurring skeleton:**\n\n| Slot | Platform | Pillar | Format |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Mon | LinkedIn | B (lessons) | text post / mini-story |\n| Wed | LinkedIn | C (POV) | contrarian post |\n| Tue | TikTok | A (build log) | talking-head storytime |\n| Fri | LinkedIn | A (build in public) | weekly \"Build Log\" update |\n| Fri | TikTok | open | **reactive/trend slot** |\n\n**Series:** \"Build Log\" (Fri LinkedIn) — weekly build-in-public update. Anticipation + zero\ndecision fatigue.\n**Planned/reactive:** ~80/20 (the Fri TikTok is the open reactive slot).\n**Rhythm:** Mon 30-min weekly fill → `batch-content-plan`; batch-film TikToks every other week;\nkeep a 1-week buffer in WoopSocial; 10 min/day engaging.\n\n**Sample week (filled):** Mon — \"We deleted our most-requested feature. Here's what we learned.\"\n(Pillar B) · Tue — storytime version for TikTok · Wed — \"Posting daily is hurting your reach.\"\n(Pillar C) · Fri — Build Log #14 + a TikTok riding a relevant founder trend.\n\n---\n\n## Example 2 — Small team (2–3) · 3 platforms with repurposing\n\n**Capacity:** founder + a part-time editor. **Platforms:** LinkedIn, TikTok, Instagram.\n\n**Cadence:** LinkedIn 4×/week, TikTok 4×/week, Instagram 3×/week — **made feasible by repurposing**,\nnot by 11 from-scratch pieces.\n\n**Repurposing spine:** each week, **2 core ideas** → each becomes a TikTok + a Reel + a LinkedIn\npost + a carousel (via `cross-platform-repurposing`). That's most of the week from 2 origins.\n\n**Series:** \"Teardown Tuesday\" (TikTok + Reel) — critique one thing weekly. \"#FixItFriday\"\n(carousel) — one mistake + the fix.\n\n**Skeleton (abbreviated):** Mon LinkedIn POV · Tue Teardown (TikTok+Reel) · Wed LinkedIn teaching\n+ carousel · Thu TikTok tip · Fri #FixItFriday carousel + LinkedIn build-update · one open reactive\nslot.\n\n**Rhythm:** monthly planning (anchors + arcs) → weekly fill → `batch-content-plan`; editor batches\nedits Thu; buffer = 1 week; founder engages daily. Roles: founder creates + engages, editor edits +\nschedules.\n\n---\n\n## Contrast — the over-ambitious calendar (do NOT do this)\n\n- **5 posts/day across 6 platforms**, all original, solo founder.\n- Every slot pre-locked for 90 days, no reactive room.\n- No buffer, no series, no repurposing — pure from-scratch volume.\n\n→ Sustained for ~2 weeks, then abandoned. The fix: cut to 1–2 platforms, a sustainable floor,\nrepurposing, a series or two, reactive room, and a buffer. A calendar you keep beats a calendar\nthat impresses on paper.\n\n---\n\n## What the good examples share\n\n- **Cadence sized to capacity** (the floor, not the ceiling).\n- A **recurring skeleton** of buckets (pillar × format × slot), not a one-off list.\n- **One or two named series** for anticipation + less decision fatigue.\n- **Reactive room** (~20–30%) and sensible **anchors**.\n- A **planning rhythm + buffer**, and clean hand-offs to `batch-content-plan` and the content skills.\n- Multi-platform made feasible by **repurposing**, not heroics. No analytics claims.\n"
